{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794337567,"nonce":"8Gc4uiKreFxJlqBeD5nibtbeVXw=","message":"Seven single-variant shaders ported (f29434644ea8468bdd8bcdf7b8785ca0d1d22a5b): shadow depth, tonemap, bloom, skybox, OIT composite, damage-rect clear, backdrop rows (src/shaders_russl, with a shared fullscreen-triangle library). Each matched its hand-written WGSL pixel for pixel (depth for the shadow pass) before the swap; after it the tests check the pixels against the same maths on the CPU (ACES curve, Kawase taps, blur weights, OIT average and coverage, depth interpolation). The mutation check found two weak probes in the OIT test, which are now strengthened. Not covered by any recorded component or UI snapshot: tonemap, bloom, skybox, OIT and the shadow pass only run in 3D scenes, so the CPU-reference tests and the mesh tests are their guard. canvas.wgsl and backdrop.wgsl are not ported: canvas is spliced with user-supplied WGSL at run time (like custom passes), and backdrop is generated by build.rs from the shared prelude. Left: text, image and path (with _dt variants), backdrop, the glass family, mesh, particles, the inline filters in shaders.rs, and the core and notch fallback tiers.","files":null}]}